# Copy to .env (or rely on the repo-root .env — this server auto-loads the first
# .env it finds walking up from mcp/youtube-mcp/).
#
# Add as many keys as you have — the server rotates through ALL of them and
# only errors when every key is quota-exhausted for the day.
# Each YouTube Data API v3 key = 10,000 units/day. search = 100 units/call,
# most other reads = 1 unit. So ~2 keys ≈ 200 searches/day + thousands of reads.

YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_API_KEY_2=
YOUTUBE_API_KEY_3=
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY_4=
# ...or one line:  YOUTUBE_API_KEYS=key1,key2,key3

# Optional shared-secret gate for the public URL. If set, every request must
# send  Authorization: Bearer <value>  OR  ?token=<value>  on the /mcp URL.
# MCP_BEARER_TOKEN=

# --- TRANSCRIPT PROXY (needed only when the server runs on a CLOUD IP) ---
# YouTube blocks the transcript endpoint from datacenter IPs (Render/AWS/GCP/
# Azure). Data API tools are unaffected. To make get_transcript /
# get_clean_transcript / search_transcript work from a cloud host, route them
# through a residential proxy — set ONE of:
#   WEBSHARE_PROXY_USERNAME=...          # Webshare "Residential" plan
#   WEBSHARE_PROXY_PASSWORD=...
# or
#   YT_PROXY_URL=http://user:pass@host:port   # any residential/rotating proxy
# (If you run this locally instead, from a home IP, no proxy is needed.)

# MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MCP_PORT=8765
